      "maintainer_comments": [
        {
          "author": "vng",
          "body": "Before going further, let's discuss and agree with some constraints:\r\n\r\nhighway=* - is the primary type for the roads in our classifier. I don't see a reason why we will have several highway=* types for one Feature, probably except the case: highway=footway + highway=cycleway, like here https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/File:Radweg_Schee_Silschede_cut.jpg\r\n\r\nSo my vision was like having _main_ type highway=* and other types define bicycle(footway) infra like: cyclewaytag=* or footwaytag=*. Again, I'm ok with the footway + cycleway exception at the same time.\r\n\r\nAgree here? So, I'm probably ok with ```extra_tag``` selector, but lets keep it as reasonable as possible.\r\n\r\nAnd rendering example:\r\n- highway=cycleway is rendered like _core_ line.\r\n- cyclewaytag=* is rendered with an _offset_ line. E.g highway=seconday + cyclewaytag=* (left, right, both) can be nicely rendered even in the generic style.",
          "url": "https://github.com/organicmaps/organicmaps/pull/14040#issuecomment-6523827420"
        }
      ]
    },
